          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Founding of the Kinsey Institute</strong><br>\nTo further his research, Kinsey founded the Institute for Sex Research at Indiana University in 1947, which later became known as the Kinsey Institute. The institute aimed to continue the study of sexology and provide education in the field.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Society and Controversy</strong><br>\nKinsey's work had a profound impact on society by challenging conventional beliefs about sexuality and opening the door to more open discussions on the subject. However, his research methods and findings were also met with controversy and criticism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Methodology and Data Collection</strong><br>\nKinsey developed a methodology for gathering data on sexual behavior, which included detailed personal histories. His Kinsey Scale, which describes a range of sexual orientations, is still used today as a framework for understanding sexual identity.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
