            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Legacy in Sexology</strong><br>\nDespite the controversy, Kinsey is regarded as a pioneer in the field of sexology. His willingness to address taboo subjects and promote sex education laid the groundwork for future research and shifted public discourse on sexual norms and morality.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Challenges and Kinsey's Personal Life</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Kinsey faced challenges, including accusations of obscenity and backlash from conservative sectors. His personal life, including his own sexual orientation and practices, has been the subject of interest and debate.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nKinsey died on August 25, 1956. His work continues to be influential in the fields of biology and sexology, with the Kinsey Institute remaining a leading organization in sexual research, education, and therapy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
